{#- The text card, as a host draws it beside `find_text`, `open_library_text` or
    `search_sources` (design.md §12, "A card in someone else's chat", 2026-10-06).

    One document with its style and script inline, handed over whole as the resource
    `ui://targum/text-card.html`, on the build card's bridge (`card-bridge.js`). The only
    words it starts with are its labels; every text it shows comes in from the tool
    result (`card-text.js`).

    It fetches nothing but a recording, and only when the reader presses Listen on a text
    that already has one (§12's second exception): the one `<audio>` below has no address
    until then; and a library text's cover from our own `/cover/` (§12, "A card's picture
    comes from targum.page", 2026-10-09). No control here starts, confirms or spends anything. A door opens a page
    of ours: the text, the library page where it is got ready, or, for an article a
    publisher put out, the add page with its address in the box. -#}
{% from '_card_head.html.j2' import head %}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
<title>{{ t("card.text.title", "Something to read") }}</title>
<style>{{ asset('card.css') }}</style>
</head>
<body>
<main class="cards" id="cards" aria-live="polite"
  data-open="{{ t("card.text.open", "Open") }}"
  data-library="{{ t("card.text.library", "Open in the library") }}"
  data-read-on="{{ t("card.text.read-on", "Read on targum") }}"
  data-watch-on="{{ t("card.text.watch-on", "Watch on targum") }}"
  data-listen-on="{{ t("card.text.listen-on", "Listen on targum") }}"
  data-listen="{{ t("reader.page.listen", "Listen") }}"
  data-pause="{{ t("card.text.pause", "Pause") }}"
  data-read-by="{{ t("card.text.read-by", "Read by {who}") }}"
  data-minutes="{{ t("library.minutes", "{n} min") }}"
  data-found="{{ t("card.text.found", "Today's news") }}"
  data-kinds='{{ kinds|tojson }}'
  data-tenths="{{ tenths }}"
  data-pace="{{ pace }}">
  <p class="card-said card-none" id="none" hidden>{{ t("card.text.none", "Nothing matched.") }}</p>
  {#- One card, its head and a row for each text (design.md §12, "The connector's pages
      are the boards'", 2026-10-09), where each text was a card of its own. -#}
  <section class="card card-sheet" id="sheet" hidden>
    {% call head() %}<span class="card-kind" id="kind">{{ t("card.text.title", "Something to read") }}</span>{% endcall %}
    <div class="card-rows" id="rows"></div>
  </section>
</main>
<template id="one">
  <article class="card-text">
    {#- The letter on the colour of its kind first; a library text's cover from
        `/cover/` replaces it once it has loaded, and never otherwise (§12, "A card's
        picture comes from targum.page"). -#}
    <span class="card-tile" aria-hidden="true"><span class="card-letter"></span></span>
    <div class="card-body">
      <h2 class="card-title" dir="auto"></h2>
      <p class="card-english" hidden></p>
      <p class="card-facts" hidden><span class="card-kind-word" hidden></span><span class="card-from" hidden></span><span class="card-minutes" hidden></span><span class="card-known" hidden></span></p>
      <span class="card-credit" hidden></span>
    </div>
    <div class="card-actions">
      <button type="button" class="card-play" aria-pressed="false" hidden>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
          <path class="play" d="M5 3.2 12.8 8 5 12.8Z"></path>
          <path class="pause" d="M5.5 3.8v8.4M10.5 3.8v8.4"></path>
        </svg>
        <span class="card-play-word"></span>
      </button>
      <a class="card-door" target="_blank" rel="noopener" hidden></a>
    </div>
  </article>
</template>
{#- The door's arrow (§7: 16px, a stroke at 1.4, round caps): out of this frame, to a
    page of ours. Cloned after the door's word, so the word stays the door's whole text. -#}
<template id="arrow"><svg class="card-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M6.5 3.5h6v6M12.5 3.5 4 12"></path></svg></template>
<audio id="ear" preload="none"></audio>
<script>{{ asset('card-bridge.js') }}</script>
<script>{{ asset('card-text.js') }}</script>
</body>
</html>
